                              "disease_code":  "VASCULAR_DEMENTIA",
                              "distinguishing_feature":  "Vascular dementia has stepwise deterioration with vascular risk factors and evidence of cerebrovascular disease on MRI; Alzheimer\u0027s has gradual insidious onset predominantly affecting episodic memory."
                          },
                          {
                              "disease_code":  "DELIRIUM",
                              "distinguishing_feature":  "Delirium is acute onset with fluctuating course and an identifiable precipitant; Alzheimer\u0027s dementia is slowly progressive over months to years without acute fluctuation."
                          },
                          {
                              "disease_code":  "DEPRESSION_PSEUDODEMENTIA",
                              "distinguishing_feature":  "Depression in elderly patients can mimic dementia (\u0027pseudodementia\u0027) with cognitive complaints, withdrawal, and poor concentration. Mood-first presentation, preserved memory on testing, and response to antidepressants distinguish depression."
                          }
